# Subagent model inheritance

When calling the Task tool (subagents):

- Do **not** set `model` unless the user explicitly names a model for that subagent.
- Omit `model` so the subagent inherits the parent agent’s model.
- Never pick `gpt-5.6-*`, Claude, Composer, or other models on your own — including for `/simplify`, reviews, explore-style work, or parallel helpers.
- If a command says “use the same model as the parent,” that means omit `model`, not choose a different slug from the allowlist.

```text
❌ BAD — invented model choice
Task(..., model: "gpt-5.6-terra-medium")

✅ GOOD — inherit parent
Task(...)   // no model field
```
